<title>USA: Uzbekistan, Belarus upgrade nuclear controls.</title>
<headline>Uzbekistan, Belarus upgrade nuclear controls.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Energy Department completed upgrading facilities in Belarus and Uzbekistan to help the former Soviet republics protect and keep track of nuclear materials, the department said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The control and accounting safeguards installed at the Sosny Science and Technical Centre in Belarus and the Uzbekistan Academy of Sciences Institute of Nuclear Physics would &quot;significantly reduce the risk of theft of bomb-grade materials at the facilities,&quot; U.S. Energy Secretary Hazel O'Leary said in a statement.</p>
<p>U.S. experts are working on similar projects at more than 40 facilities in Russia, Kazakhstan and Ukraine, and completed security work at a nuclear research centre in Latvia last March.</p>
